\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Nearest neighbors are not rescaled twice}
\date{2026-11-06}

\p{If #{R=1} and #{c_1=1}, then #{\alpha(\theta)=2(1-\cos\theta)}
and #{\kappa=1}. The
[finite-range circle precision](fdip-00C8) is then the matrix
of the [circle mesh](fdip-004H). In \ref{fdip-004I} the
exponent is #{f^TQ_Nf/(2N)}, so the raw covariance of that
published field is #{NQ_N^{-1}}. By \ref{fdip-000B}, the counting-coordinate field
of precision #{Q_N} has covariance #{Q_N^{-1}}. Multiplication
by #{\sqrt{\kappa N}} matches the published field when
#{\kappa=1}. For the nearest-neighbor choice that factor
equals #{\sqrt{N}}, and the published field is not multiplied
by a further #{\sqrt{N}}.}
